WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.600
Active footprints are created when a person or organization intentionally publishes or

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.875
submits information.

00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:11.120
Posts, public profiles, comments, photographs, videos, resumes, websites, press releases,

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.280
issue discussions, and public repositories can all become durable and searchable.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.670
Intentional sharing does not mean every future use was expected.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.920
A post written for one audience may be copied, archived, indexed,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.160
or viewed years later in a different context.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.694
Edits and deletion can reduce exposure but may not remove prior copies or references.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:32.385
Passive footprints arise through collection, observation, and technical operation.

00:00:32.385 --> 00:00:34.640
Services generate access and security logs.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.415
Websites and applications may use analytics or tracking.

00:00:37.415 --> 00:00:39.040
Search engines index pages.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.474
Data brokers compile records.

00:00:40.474 --> 00:00:45.080
Breach notifications may indicate that account data was exposed by a compromised provider.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.240
People and organizations often underestimate passive exposure because it is distributed

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.255
across many systems and controlled by third parties.

00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:56.265
Settings may be complex, retention may be unclear, and one service can combine account,

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:58.320
device, location, and behavioral data.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.275
The boundary is not always perfect.

00:01:00.275 --> 00:01:01.960
Uploading a photograph is active,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.595
while embedded metadata or subsequent indexing may be passive.

00:01:05.595 --> 00:01:06.800
Creating an account is deliberate,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.325
while the service's long-term logging and profiling may not be obvious to the user.

00:01:11.325 --> 00:01:13.510
Managing both types requires awareness and control.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:17.400
Limit intentional publication to what is necessary, review account and service settings,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.400
secure accounts, understand important third-party practices,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.280
and monitor for unexpected exposure.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.300
Do not assume that invisible collection is harmless or that deliberate sharing remains

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.000
under the original publisher's control.
